ty acids, induce the expression of cyclooxygenase-2 mediated through Toll-like receptor 4</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2001</year><volume>276</volume><fpage>16683</fpage><lpage>16689</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||276|16683||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11278967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Le Guevel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pakdel</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessment of oestrogenic potency of chemicals used as growth promoter by <italic>in-vitro</italic> methods</article-title><source>Hum Reprod</source><year>2001</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1030</fpage><lpage>1036</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Hum Reprod||16|1030||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11331656</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mitra</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Faruque</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><name><surname>Avis</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Breast cancer and environmental risks: where is the link</article-title><source>J Environ Health</source><year>2004</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>24</fpage><lpage>32</lpage>40; quiz 41-2<!--PubMed citation query: 'J Environ Health||66|24||bib17|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>National Food Administration</collab></person-group><article-title/><source>Food Composition Tables</source><year>1989</year><publisher-name>Publisher: National Food Administration: Uppsala</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pousette</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><